{
  "dom_id": "step-q115899",
  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${x}^{2}=8y?$",
  "worked_solution": "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at the origin is\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4(2)y.\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=2.$ Therefore, our parabola has its vertex at $(0,0).$",
